---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Devina Azaria — Science, Engineering & Aerospace">
<section class="shell hero">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Student Portfolio · Yogyakarta, Indonesia</div>
    <h1>Science.<br/>Engineering.<br/>Aerospace.</h1>
    <p class="lead">I’m Devina Azaria, a high school student exploring how scientific thinking, engineering, and creative practice can turn curiosity into real projects.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#projects">Explore Projects</a><a class="button secondary" href="#academic">Academic Journey</a></div>
  </div>
  <aside class="panel">
    <div class="tag">Current Direction</div>
    <div class="big">From science foundations to aerospace engineering.</div>
    <p class="muted">Astronomy and olympiad learning strengthen the science base; engineering projects will progressively document design, testing, iteration, and reflection.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<section id="projects" class="shell section">
  <div class="eyebrow">Projects</div>
  <h2>Evidence over claims.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Projects are documented through the problem, process, tools, result, evidence, and reflection.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><div class="tag">Learning System</div><h3>Olympiad Learning System</h3><p class="muted">A structured framework for olympiad preparation, beginning with Astronomy & Astrophysics as a reference pilot.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="tag">Engineering</div><h3>Engineering Projects</h3><p class="muted">Upcoming hands-on builds will focus on mechanics, measurement, prototyping, testing, and clear technical documentation.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="tag">Research</div><h3>Scientific Thinking</h3><p class="muted">Small research investigations will be used to practice asking measurable questions, analyzing evidence, and communicating findings.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="academic" class="shell section">
  <div class="eyebrow">Academic Direction</div>
  <h2>Building the foundation.</h2>
  <div class="timeline">
    <div class="step"><strong>Science</strong><br/><span class="muted">Mathematics, physics, astronomy, and olympiad reasoning.</span></div>
    <div class="step"><strong>Engineering</strong><br/><span class="muted">Mechanics, design thinking, coding, prototyping, and experimentation.</span></div>
    <div class="step"><strong>Aerospace</strong><br/><span class="muted">A long-term direction connecting physics and engineering to flight and space systems.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="achievements" class="shell section">
  <div class="eyebrow">Achievements & Activities</div>
  <h2>A broad learning profile.</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><h3>Academic Competitions</h3><p class="muted">Experience across science, mathematics, English, language, and olympiad-style competitions.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Leadership & School Life</h3><p class="muted">Participation in student organizations, collaborative activities, and school-based creative initiatives.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Culture & Communication</h3><p class="muted">Traditional arts, storytelling, public performance, and cultural activities complement the technical journey.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="beyond" class="shell section">
  <div class="eyebrow">Beyond STEM</div>
  <h2>Music and culture shape how I create.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Drums, violin, guitar, vocal performance, macapat, geguritan, and collaborative music projects are part of the same habit: listening closely, practicing deliberately, and improving through iteration.</p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>